{"parentUuid":"7fd606c8-bf0f-4e0c-a6d8-25a11dc46603","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1K9p85zoyqxhjCYNe7E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KtuXCUuq32hSQ4cPDfgUhE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\tool-results\\bzhr1r7s5.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":158899,"output_tokens":135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1056},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":158899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1056,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KtuXCUuq32hSQ4cPDfgUhE":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\tool-results\\bzhr1r7s5.txt"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b9964f4b-cdad-496d-9b85-63764bc5e332","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg1K9orxmsVWapKJZWouF","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"56fa02dd-d1af-41b9-8c51-7531eeacdb23","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:07:58.317Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"56fa02dd-d1af-41b9-8c51-7531eeacdb23","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0670f495-d42b-47ba-a2cb-691fa22a4834","agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtuXCUuq32hSQ4cPDfgUhE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t########## 01-decisions-and-rules.md ##########\n2\t--- docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md\t2026-10-08 05:50:48.560112800 -0400\n3\t+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:25.967579500 -0400\n4\t@@ -1,29 +1,36 @@\n5\t-# Decisions and rules\n6\t-\n7\t-## Core directive (check every feature against this)\n8\t-\n9\t-CUORE is a diagnostic assistant for a mechanic who specialises in one brand and model. Its job is to help him diagnose this car on evidence, prove the repair, and make the next same-model car with the same fault start from what this one taught. The mechanic decides; CUORE advises and records, with sources, dates and confidence. Before building anything, ask: does it serve diagnosing, proving, or learning for the next car? If not, do not build it. No boards, throughput, blocking gates or inventory management.\n10\t-\n11\t-## Owner's standing rules (2026-09 to 2026-10)\n12\t-\n13\t-1. The mechanic makes the decisions and the repairs. CUORE supplies the most recent, truthful information with date, source and confidence, labels stale or unverified items, and never invents values.\n14\t-2. Others' experience matters: every code, family and job carries verified YouTube how-tos and direct forum threads. Forums block plain HTTP checks, so links are verified through a real browser (headless Edge over the DevTools Protocol).\n15\t-3. Images (photos, scans, borescope video) and audio clips (what a bearing sounds and feels like) are first-class evidence: easy to upload, keep, search and recover.\n16\t-4. Parts need full detail and images; part sites block automated image checks, so images are verified through the browser and linked, never copied.\n17\t-5. More interactivity: the mechanic can correct, question, confirm or add input on any fact and see the answer; an Inbox per car tracks it.\n18\t-6. Systems (25 of them, electrical first) are a correlational dimension for every issue: code to system mapping, dependencies, co-occurrence over time, and the physical layout (wiring, connectors, grounds, boxes, components, locations, conditions) per problem.\n19\t-7. Align CUORE with a mechanic's technical tool like MultiEcuScan: one logical flow tying driver input, mechanic input, test results and malfunctions together (Job workflow, MES-style Modules view).\n20\t-8. Printed pages and PDFs must be properly formatted, with an \"as of\" stamp and sources.\n21\t-9. Branding: Alfa Romeo first; later ported to Alfa, Maserati and Ferrari. Keep marque specifics in data and config. The Stelvio's sibling cars are the Maserati Grecale (shares the Giorgio platform and GME 2.0T engine family) and Levante (different platform, component-level overlap only).\n22\t-10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n23\t-\n24\t-## Design decisions\n25\t-\n26\t-- Safety: no HTTP route ever writes to the car. Clears, actuator tests and routines are MCP-only, need an exact consent phrase (CLEAR <MODULE>, ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>, RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>), and are refused on blocked modules (ABS, EPS, ORC, HALF, DASM, ESL, TVM, TCM, ESM, DTCM, RFHUB, anything on CAN-CH). The live poller only reads (OBD Mode 01/03/07, UDS 0x22) and every other adapter operation is refused while it holds the port.\n27\t-- Evidence: the evidence gate counts only measurements from the car (serial stream). Replay, demo, snapshots, symptoms, notes, feedback, media and inspections are labelled and excluded as measurements. Clearing is not fixing: the verdict stays \"unverified repair\" until a readiness read from the car shows the monitor complete with no code back.\n28\t-- Verdict and status are computed, never hand-written: ACTIVE FAULTS, UNVERIFIED REPAIR, VERIFIED CLEAN, NO DATA; per code ACTIVE, CLEARED UNVERIFIED, STALE.\n29\t-- Known-good bands: only one-sided limits (too hot) become gauge warn/alarm bands; idle-only or two-sided ranges show as notes; UNKNOWN stays blank.\n30\t-- Dossier structure (from the mechanic UX review, implemented 2026-10-07): verdict first, open-work job cards with shared tick state, everything else collapsed with counts, one sticky strip of about 104 px, 16 px body, 44 px targets, dark theme toggle, quick-add note button.\n31\t-- Family findings: several EVAP codes are one fault; three or more lost-communication codes are one power or bus event (supply and grounds first).\n32\t-- Recordings stay in MultiEcuScan's CSV format so the existing log tools read them unchanged.\n33\t-- CUORE runs offline on loopback, kept alive by a per-user scheduled task; no network or Claude dependency.\n34\t+# Decisions and rules\n35\t+\n36\t+## Core directive (check every feature against this)\n37\t+\n38\t+CUORE is a diagnostic assistant for a mechanic who specialises in one brand and model. Its job is to help him diagnose this car on evidence, prove the repair, and make the next same-model car with the same fault start from what this one taught. The mechanic decides; CUORE advises and records, with sources, dates and confidence. Before building anything, ask: does it serve diagnosing, proving, or learning for the next car? If not, do not build it. No boards, throughput, blocking gates or inventory management.\n39\t+\n40\t+## Owner's standing rules (2026-09 to 2026-10)\n41\t+\n42\t+1. The mechanic makes the decisions and the repairs. CUORE supplies the most recent, truthful information with date, source and confidence, labels stale or unverified items, and never invents values.\n43\t+2. Others' experience matters: every code, family and job carries verified YouTube how-tos and direct forum threads. Forums block plain HTTP checks, so links are verified through a real browser (headless Edge over the DevTools Protocol).\n44\t+3. Images (photos, scans, borescope video) and audio clips (what a bearing sounds and feels like) are first-class evidence: easy to upload, keep, search and recover.\n45\t+4. Parts need full detail and images; part sites block automated image checks, so images are verified through the browser and linked, never copied.\n46\t+5. More interactivity: the mechanic can correct, question, confirm or add input on any fact and see the answer; an Inbox per car tracks it.\n47\t+6. Systems (25 of them, electrical first) are a correlational dimension for every issue: code to system mapping, dependencies, co-occurrence over time, and the physical layout (wiring, connectors, grounds, boxes, components, locations, conditions) per problem.\n48\t+7. Align CUORE with a mechanic's technical tool like MultiEcuScan: one logical flow tying driver input, mechanic input, test results and malfunctions together (Job workflow, MES-style Modules view).\n49\t+8. Printed pages and PDFs must be properly formatted, with an \"as of\" stamp and sources.\n50\t+9. Branding: Alfa Romeo first; later ported to Alfa, Maserati and Ferrari. Keep marque specifics in data and config. The Stelvio's sibling cars are the Maserati Grecale (shares the Giorgio platform and GME 2.0T engine family) and Levante (different platform, component-level overlap only).\n51\t+10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n52\t+\n53\t+## Owner's standing rules added 2026-10-13\n54\t+\n55\t+11. Fable (the top-level model) does analysis and decisions only -- it never builds. All building goes to Sonnet/Haiku agents, at most about five running concurrently, and the whole working set stays at roughly half the main model's own token budget. (Also in Claude memory: \"Low-cost subagents only\" -- haiku/sonnet for Agent calls, never Fable forks.)\n56\t+12. About ten complete (full-vehicle) scans over the course of one diagnosis is the right order of magnitude -- not one scan per question. One guided scan (the `/coverage` cable wizard, or a full scan) per shop visit, not per code or per hypothesis.\n57\t+13. Mobile is held to the same standard as the main app: the Ferrari benchmark, not a form. Design and finish matter there exactly as much as on the bench pages -- dark theme, an intro reveal on every open, a camera on every form, prestige over utility-app defaults. (Tell CUORE's first pass was rejected and rebuilt to this standard, 2026-10-13.)\n58\t+14. The photo-reading (vision) provider stays off by default (`CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=none`) because CUORE runs offline by rule. Turning on the `claude` provider is the owner's own explicit, informed opt-in -- it is the one path in the app that deliberately leaves the LAN and sends data (a photo) to Anthropic -- never a default, never silently enabled by another feature.\n59\t+\n60\t+## Design decisions\n61\t+\n62\t+- Safety: no HTTP route ever writes to the car. Clears, actuator tests and routines are MCP-only, need an exact consent phrase (CLEAR <MODULE>, ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>, RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>), and are refused on blocked modules (ABS, EPS, ORC, HALF, DASM, ESL, TVM, TCM, ESM, DTCM, RFHUB, anything on CAN-CH). The live poller only reads (OBD Mode 01/03/07, UDS 0x22) and every other adapter operation is refused while it holds the port.\n63\t+- Evidence: the evidence gate counts only measurements from the car (serial stream). Replay, demo, snapshots, symptoms, notes, feedback, media and inspections are labelled and excluded as measurements. Clearing is not fixing: the verdict stays \"unverified repair\" until a readiness read from the car shows the monitor complete with no code back.\n64\t+- Verdict and status are computed, never hand-written: ACTIVE FAULTS, UNVERIFIED REPAIR, VERIFIED CLEAN, NO DATA; per code ACTIVE, CLEARED UNVERIFIED, STALE.\n65\t+- Known-good bands: only one-sided limits (too hot) become gauge warn/alarm bands; idle-only or two-sided ranges show as notes; UNKNOWN stays blank.\n66\t+- Dossier structure (from the mechanic UX review, implemented 2026-10-07): verdict first, open-work job cards with shared tick state, everything else collapsed with counts, one sticky strip of about 104 px, 16 px body, 44 px targets, dark theme toggle, quick-add note button.\n67\t+- Family findings: several EVAP codes are one fault; three or more lost-communication codes are one power or bus event (supply and grounds first).\n68\t+- Recordings stay in MultiEcuScan's CSV format so the existing log tools read them unchanged.\n69\t+- CUORE runs offline on loopback, kept alive by a per-user scheduled task; no network or Claude dependency.\n70\t\n71\t########## 02-architecture.md ##########\n72\t--- docs/handbook/02-architecture.md\t2026-10-07 23:28:56.695246000 -0400\n73\t+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/02-architecture.md\t2026-10-13 22:04:48.174823800 -0400\n74\t@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n75\t # Architecture\n76\t \n77\t-Generated from the code on 2026-10-07. Re-run the greps noted inline if this drifts.\n78\t+Generated from the code on 2026-10-07, refreshed 2026-10-13. Re-run the greps noted inline if this drifts.\n79\t \n80\t ## The three programs\n81\t \n82\t@@ -64,13 +64,27 @@\n83\t | Report | `/v/{vin}/report` | `cuore/web/report_routes.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `timeline_bridge`, `experience_bridge`, `parts_bridge` | `report.html` | `cuore/tests/check_report.py` |\n84\t | Inbox | `/v/{vin}/inbox` | `cuore/web/inbox_routes.py` | `feedback_bridge` | `inbox.html`, `_feedback_panel.html` | `cuore/tests/check_feedback_page.py`, `check_feedback.py` |\n85\t | Logs (link, not a `/v/` tab) | `/logs?vin={vin}` | `cuore/web/routes.py` | `mes_bridge` | `logs.html` | -- |\n86\t+| Tests (2026-10-08, visible tab) | `/v/{vin}/tests` | `cuore/web/tests_routes.py` | `tests_bridge` (via `GET /api/tests/{vin}`) | `tests.html` | `cuore/tests/check_tests_page.py` |\n87\t+| Scans (2026-10-13) | `/v/{vin}/scans`, `/v/{vin}/scans/{scan_id}` | `cuore/web/scanlog_routes.py` | `scanlog_bridge` over `cuore/live/scanlog.py` (groups `observations.jsonl` into sessions, writes nothing) | `scanlog.html`, `scan.html` | `cuore/tests/check_scanlog_page.py` |\n88\t+| Health report (2026-10-13, link from Scans, not its own vbar tab) | `/v/{vin}/health`, `/v/{vin}/scans/{scan_id}/health` | `cuore/web/scan_health_routes.py` | `scan_health_bridge` | `scan_health.html` | `cuore/tests/check_scan_health.py` |\n89\t \n90\t-Not on the vbar but under `/v/{vin}/...`: `verify` (`dossier_routes.py`), `oil-change`/`service`/`brakes-tires`/`torque`/`maintenance` (`service_routes.py`), `drivetrain/{section}` (`drivetrain_routes.py`), `labels`/`labels.pdf` (`labels_routes.py`), `notes` (`routes.py`), `dealer` (`routes.py`), `live-vs-log` (`routes.py`).\n91\t+Vehicle tab strip is now `cuore/web/templates/_vtabs.html` (included from `_vbar.html`), not the old inline list: visible row is Bench, Job, Codes, Live (liveboard), Tests, Systems, Report, Mobile; everything else (Dossier, Modules, Timeline, Gauges, Electrical, Parts, Media, Service, Fault tree, Evidence gate, Inbox, Labels, Logs, Scans, Dashboard, plus a plain link to Tell CUORE) sits behind \"More...\". Health report and the Systems dive-in (`/v/{vin}/systems/{key}`, below) are reached by links from Scans/Systems, not tab entries of their own.\n92\t+\n93\t+Not on the vbar but under `/v/{vin}/...`: `verify` (`dossier_routes.py`), `oil-change`/`service`/`brakes-tires`/`torque`/`maintenance` (`service_routes.py`), `drivetrain/{section}` (`drivetrain_routes.py`), `labels`/`labels.pdf` (`labels_routes.py`), `notes` (`routes.py`), `dealer` (`routes.py`), `live-vs-log` (`routes.py`), `systems/{key}` (`cuore/web/system_routes.py` -- Systems dive-in phase 1, per-system status/relationship ring/fault tree page built from `cuore/services/system_detail_bridge.py`).\n94\t+\n95\t+## Mobile companion: Tell CUORE (`/m/{vin}`), 2026-10-13\n96\t+\n97\t+`cuore/web/owner_routes.py` -- its own phone-first layout (own `Jinja2Templates`, `m_*.html` templates, no desktop chrome), rebuilt 2026-10-13 to the \"Ferrari benchmark\" (dark, intro reveal every open, hero with odometer/verdict, four quick actions, 3-tap fill-up, camera on every form). Routes: `GET /m/{vin}`, `/add`, `/add/{category}`, `/add/{category}/{kind}` (+ `POST`), `/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}`, `/snap` (+ `POST`), `/messages` (+ reply `POST`), `/history`, `/qr`.\n98\t+\n99\t+Every record it writes is **attested, never a car measurement** -- backed by `cuore/live/owner_events.py` (taxonomy: 9 categories, 62 kinds) via `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`, exposed at `/api/owner/{vin}/taxonomy`, `/events` (GET/POST), `/messages` (GET, reply POST), `/correlations` (`cuore/api/owner_events.py`). No route in this chain ever reaches `cuore.live.actuate`/`clear`/`learn`.\n100\t+\n101\t+\"Snap & fill\" photo reading: `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` (`cuore/api/vision.py` -> `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py`), provider `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` = `none` (default, offline) | `claude` (opt-in, sends the photo to Anthropic) | `tesseract` (probe stub, nothing installed). Every value returned is a suggestion a human confirms; a confirmed value saved from a photo is stamped `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`. `docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md` is the documented contract for a future Swift/Flutter app, guarded by `check_api_contract.py`.\n102\t \n103\t ## API router files (`cuore/api/*.py`)\n104\t \n105\t | File | Prefix | Purpose (from docstring) |\n106\t |---|---|---|\n107\t+| `cases.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /vehicles/{vin}/cases/match`, `/cases/prefill` -- case memory read-only, via `cases_bridge` -> `mes.cases` |\n108\t | `checklists.py` | `/api` | Shop-visible checklist state over HTTP: GET/POST one step at a time |\n109\t | `deps.py` | n/a | Shared route dependencies (the single shared-token auth) |\n110\t | `dossier.py` | `/api` | `GET /api/vehicles/{vin}/view` -- the redesigned dossier's data as JSON, read-only |\n111\t@@ -79,18 +93,61 @@\n112\t | `feedback.py` | `/api` | Mechanic feedback on a fact cuore showed; mirrors the MCP feedback tools call-for-call |\n113\t | `jobs.py` | `/api` | JSON face of the Job (case) workflow; writes are thin pass-through to the bridge |\n114\t | `known_good.py` | `/api` | `GET /api/live/known-good`: known-good reference bands for live channels |\n115\t-| `live.py` | `/api` | The live link over HTTP; no write route, read-only UDS allowlist enforced |\n116\t+| `live.py` | `/api` | The live link over HTTP; no write route, read-only UDS allowlist enforced; also hosts `/live/fullscan`, `/live/fullscan/last`, `/live/capture`, `/live/learn/*` (below) |\n117\t | `live_ui.py` | `/api` | Layouts, replay, custom channels, snapshots and triggers for the live-data dashboard UI |\n118\t | `logs.py` | `/api` | Raw log access: index, one file verbatim, regex search (filename-resolution security note) |\n119\t | `media.py` | `/api` | Mechanic evidence media library: upload, browse, recover photos/scans/clips |\n120\t+| `owner_events.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | HTTP face of Tell CUORE (`/owner/{vin}/taxonomy`, `/events`, `/messages`, `/correlations`); every row attested, no route reaches the car |\n121\t | `parts.py` | `/api` | Parts catalog (names, numbers, supersessions, torque, price, images) |\n122\t | `recordings.py` | `/api` | CSV recordings from MES's graph subsystem; only MES output with real per-sample timestamps |\n123\t | `reference.py` | `/api` | Static reference data: module registry and failure-type table |\n124\t+| `scan_health.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /scans/{vin}/{scan_id}/health`(`.md`), `POST .../health/save` -- the scan health report, via `scan_health_bridge` |\n125\t+| `scanlog.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /{vin}/diff`, `/{vin}/{scan_id}`, `/{vin}/{scan_id}/export` -- one scan in full or diffed, exported as JSON or an MES-style log; the only writer, and only under `CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/` |\n126\t | `system.py` | `/api` | Capabilities, health and corpus status; `/api/capabilities` is the first call any client makes |\n127\t | `systems.py` | `/api` | Vehicle-systems graph and DTC-system correlation |\n128\t+| `systems_map.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /systems/{vin}/state` (Systems map overlay: per-system colour, hot edges, session time slider) and `/systems/{vin}/live` (live overlay: worst live colour grade per system, any brand-new DTC); via `systems_map_bridge`, never writes to the car |\n129\t+| `tests.py` (2026-10-08) | `/api` | `GET /tests/catalog`, `/tests/{vin}`, `POST /tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result` -- the mechanic-test catalogue (`mes.mechanic_tests`) and per-VIN results, via `tests_bridge` |\n130\t | `timeline.py` | `/api` | Mechanic-vs-driver timeline: codes on one axis, felt symptoms on the other |\n131\t | `tools.py` | `/api` | Read-only data for the Tools catalogue page; writes to the car listed only as inert cards |\n132\t | `vehicles.py` | `/api` | Per-vehicle diagnostics: the dossier and everything it points at |\n133\t+| `vision.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /vision/status`, `POST /vision/{vin}/read` -- \"read this photo\" for Tell CUORE, via `vision_bridge`; never writes an owner event itself, never touches the car |\n134\t+\n135\t+## Full scan, bus capture and learn (`cuore/live/*`, 2026-10-13)\n136\t+\n137\t+- **Full scan** (`cuore/live/fullscan.py`, `POST /api/live/fullscan`, `GET /api/live/fullscan/last`): one read-only pass over every subsystem the adapter can reach -- OBD DTCs/readiness/Mode $06/Mode $09, every freeze-frame PID, a UDS module sweep with status flags, and a coverage rollup -- sequenced through the existing `cuore/live/ops.py` readers (no new adapter traffic of its own) and recorded as from-car observations so the Scans area, dossier and health report all see it without fifteen separate manual calls. Each step is wrapped so one failure doesn't sink the scan.\n138\t+- **Guided cable wizard** is the pre-existing `/coverage` page (`cuore/web/routes.py`, `coverage.html`, not VIN-scoped itself): a guided three-pass, three-bus session (main bus with no cable, chassis bus through the grey cable, body bus through the blue cable, main bus again) with a bystander diff, backed by `/api/live/coverage*`. Full scan's own `scan_coverage` observation and this wizard's coverage session are two different mechanisms over the same `cuore/live/coverage.py` state.\n139\t+- **Bus capture**: `POST /api/live/capture` (`cuore/live/capture.py`) listens passively (`STCMM 0`, no CAN ACK) and returns the raw frame list; it does **not** persist an observation today -- the frames go back to the caller only.\n140\t+- **Learn**: `cuore/live/learn.py` (pure functions, reconstructs ISO-TP/UDS request-response pairs and DID time series from a passive capture) + `cuore/live/learned.py` (saves accepted mappings to `learned_dids.json`), reached at `POST /api/live/learn/capture`, `/live/learn/correlate`, `/live/learn/accept`, `GET /api/live/learned` -- how a wiTECH capture becomes a DID mapping cuore can read on its own, without ever talking to the adapter itself.\n141\t+- **Live board freeze-frame panel** (`cuore/api/liveboard.py` `/liveboard/{vin}/freeze/capture|status|stop|save|discard`, `cuore/services/liveboard_bridge.py`): starts a capture of stored codes + every supported PID's freeze frame + a Mode 01 snapshot; on save, writes `obd_dtcs`, `freeze_frame`, `pid` (one per channel) and `readiness` observations and hands back a Scans-area scan id.\n142\t+\n143\t+## Observation kinds (`cuore/live/store.py:record_observation`, `observations.jsonl`)\n144\t+\n145\t+No kind is an enum -- any string is accepted; this is what the code actually writes and reads as of 2026-10-13.\n146\t+\n147\t+| Kind | Written by | Read by |\n148\t+|---|---|---|\n149\t+| `adapter_identity` | `fullscan.py` | `dossier_bridge`/health report (adapter/session context) |\n150\t+| `mode09` | `fullscan.py` | scan health report (coverage gaps) |\n151\t+| `obd_dtcs` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` (single reads), `liveboard_bridge.py` (freeze save) | `dossier_bridge`, `scan_health_bridge`, `scanlog.py` (scan grouping) |\n152\t+| `freeze_frame` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py`, `liveboard_bridge.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n153\t+| `readiness` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py`, `liveboard_bridge.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n154\t+| `mode06` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n155\t+| `pids_snapshot` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` |\n156\t+| `pid` | `liveboard_bridge.py` (freeze capture, one per channel) | `scanlog.py` (latest-value-per-PID in a window) |\n157\t+| `module_dtcs` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scan_health_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n158\t+| `module_identity` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` |\n159\t+| `did` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | scan health report (DID coverage) |\n160\t+| `scan_coverage` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` (the report's coverage section) |\n161\t+\n162\t+`capture()`'s passive bus listen is not recorded under any kind (see above) -- that is a real gap, not an undocumented one.\n163\t+\n164\t+## Case close-out (2026-10-13 commit 31c0d71)\n165\t+\n166\t+Closing a Job (`cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py:close_job`, step 12) builds and saves a Case (`mes.cases.case_from_job`/`record_case`): confirmed/ruled-out hypotheses, tests run, parts fitted, verification state, pitfalls. `mes.cases.match(vin, codes)`/`prefill(vin, codes)`, exposed read-only at `GET /api/vehicles/{vin}/cases/match` and `/cases/prefill` (`cuore/api/cases.py`, `cuore/services/cases_bridge.py` -- the only module that imports `mes.cases`), rank real recorded cases above the seed data and feed Job prefill from the Systems pages; wording always says \"on the last `<Model>` with these codes\", never presenting a prior car's fix as this car's answer.\n167\t+\n168\t+## Marque theming (`marque_for_vin`, 2026-10-13 commit 003d6a4)\n169\t+\n170\t+`cuore/web/routes.py`'s `_page()` computes `data-marque` once per request from `cuore.services.mes_bridge.marque_for_vin(vin)` (pure passthrough to `mes.platform.marque_for_vin`, confidence-graded VIN-WMI decode: `alfa`/`maserati`/`ferrari`/`unknown`, never guessed) and every `/v/{vin}/*` page inherits it from that one call, instead of each route guessing (previously `data-marque` was hardcoded to `\"alfa\"`).\n171\t \n172\t ## MCP tools\n173\t \n174\t\n175\t########## 05-methods-and-gotchas.md ##########\n176\t--- docs/handbook/05-methods-and-gotchas.md\t2026-10-13 16:59:33.582411500 -0400\n177\t+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/05-methods-and-gotchas.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:14.658971900 -0400\n178\t@@ -11,4 +11,11 @@\n179\t - Git: agent-driven `git push` is blocked by the permission classifier; the owner approves a direct `git push github main`. Remote `forge` is unrelated; never push there.\n180\t - PDF sheets: reportlab in the project venv; render with pypdfium2 and look at the PNG; one US Letter page each; generators live in `docs/vehicles/<VIN>/pdf-sources/`.\n181\t - Serving \"Tell CUORE\" (`/m/{vin}`) to a phone on the shop LAN: the bind setting is `CUORE_HOST` (`cuore/config.py`, default `127.0.0.1`), not a separate `CUORE_BIND` -- one setting already does this, so a second was not added. Setting `CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0` in the keep-alive makes the app reachable from every device on the LAN with **no authentication** unless `CUORE_TOKEN` is also set -- that is the owner's decision, not a default (see `Settings.lan_exposed`/`unguarded_lan`). `GET /m/{vin}/qr` only renders the LAN URL when `lan_exposed` is true; it prints the URL as selectable text (no `qrcode` package in this venv, and a from-scratch QR matrix generator was out of scope) rather than a QR image.\n182\t+- **Three live-layer findings from the first real bench session (2026-10-13, vLinker FS r2 / STN1170 v4.3.2), all fixed in `cuore/live/`:**\n183\t+  1. *Gateway-silent CAN-C needs an active probe.* This car's Security Gateway Module means CAN-C carries no broadcast traffic, so passive listening alone reads as a dead bus. `cuore/live/ops.py:verify_bus` now falls back to an active Mode 01 PID 00 probe (`_active_probe_0100`) before giving up, and marks the bus `verified_by=\"active_probe_0100\"` so later reads know to use the route the probe actually got an answer on.\n184\t+  2. *This car answers legislated OBD only on the 29-bit route.* `18DB33F1 -> 18DAF110` (ECM) / `18DAF118` (TCM), not the 11-bit `7DF`/`7E8` pair -- the opposite of what an earlier (2026-09-25) note on this same car assumed. `cuore/live/ops.py:_obd_route` now prefers whichever STP protocol the active probe was verified against; `cuore/live/transport.py` (session open, ~line 144) restates the 29-bit functional header via `ATCP18`/`ATSHDB33F1`/`ATSTFF` (a single 8-digit `ATSH` is silently ignored by this firmware and leaves the old header in force -- reads as NO DATA, not an error).\n185\t+  3. *`STFAC` on this STN firmware wipes the default pass filters.* After `STFAC` (used when adding custom pass filters, `cuore/live/capture.py:_add_filters`), every reply reads NO DATA because the firmware's default filters are gone too, not just overridden. Fix (`cuore/live/transport.py`, same session-open path, right after the STFAC path runs): re-issue `STCFCPC` + `STP <protocol>` to restore the defaults, then restate the functional header again -- `STP` resets it as well.\n186\t+- **An MCP server process holds the code it started with.** `obd2-mcp/server.py` and `mes-log-mcp/server.py` run as long-lived subprocesses under Claude Code's MCP connection; editing either file does not change what the running tools do until the connection is torn down and rebuilt with the `/mcp` command (reload/reconnect). A code fix that \"doesn't seem to take\" after an edit is usually this, not a real regression -- reload before re-diagnosing.\n187\t+- `cuore/services/cache.py:get_or_build(key, build)` is a small in-process memo cache (16 entries, LRU) keyed on whatever makes the value stale -- never just the VIN. The shared convention across bridges: `(\"workup\", vin, mes_bridge.newest_mtime(vin))` for anything built from the MES log corpus (used by `bench_routes.py`, `flow_bridge.py`, `tests_bridge.py`, `timeline_bridge.py`, `dossier_bridge.py`, `jobs_bridge.py` and others -- this is what took the Report page from 30 s to 5 s and the Job page from 3.2 s to 0.3 s, 2026-10-13); `(\"scan_health\", vin, scan_id, observations.jsonl's mtime)` for the scan health report (`scan_health_bridge.py:build_cached`); `(\"bench_tree_candidates\", vin, codes, mtime)` for the Bench fault-tree view. A new or edited log/observation moves the mtime key component and the stale entry simply falls out -- no invalidation hook needed, but a cache key that forgets to include the right mtime will silently serve a stale page.\n188\t+- Tell CUORE's phone URL moves with the PC's LAN address: cuore binds `CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0` (set in the launchers) and the shop PC is on DHCP, so the IP in the `/m/{vin}/qr` URL (192.168.68.80 as of 2026-10-13; was 192.168.0.161) can change on a reboot or router restart -- check the current address before handing a phone the link, don't assume last session's. The Windows Firewall rule for inbound TCP 5000 needs an admin to run once (`New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"CUORE 5000\" -Direction Inbound -Action Allow -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 5000 -Profile Any`); without it the LAN bind is correct but nothing outside the PC itself can reach the port.\n189\t - \"Read this photo\" (`POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`, `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` + `cuore/api/vision.py`): a value read from a photo is a **suggestion the human confirms**, never a car measurement -- when the confirmed value is saved as an owner event, the caller stamps `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field (same provenance convention `cuore.live.owner_events` already uses) so the record still says it came from a picture, not an instrument. Field names in the response are the real `cuore.live.owner_events.TAXONOMY` field names for the hints that map onto one kind (`fuel_pump` -> `fuel/fill_up`, `oil_bottle` -> `fluids/engine_oil_change`, `part_label` -> `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere`, `receipt` -> `fuel/fill_up`); `odometer` returns `odometer_km` with `suggested_kind: null` because that is the event's own top-level field, not a kind field. Provider is `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` (default `none`, which is deliberately the honest \"not set up, fill in by hand\" answer -- CUORE runs offline by rule, so a vision backend is never silently on). `claude` only turns on with `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` **and** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set -- that call leaves the LAN and goes to Anthropic over plain HTTPS via `urllib` (no `anthropic` SDK in this venv, and none was added), so it is the owner's explicit, informed choice, never a default. `tesseract` is a probe-only stub (`_find_tesseract` checks PATH and `C:\\Program Files\\Tesseract-OCR\\tesseract.exe`); nothing is installed there today and no OCR is wired up behind it. Tests (`cuore/tests/check_vision.py`) monkeypatch `cuore.services.vision_bridge.urllib.request.urlopen` to return a canned Messages-API body rather than calling the real network.\n190\t\n191\t########## 06-roadmap.md ##########\n192\t--- docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md\t2026-10-13 16:54:09.320387500 -0400\n193\t+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:50.319653500 -0400\n194\t@@ -1,18 +1,28 @@\n195\t # Roadmap\n196\t \n197\t-## Just built (2026-10-07), to settle in\n198\t+## Done\n199\t \n200\t-Systems layer (25 systems), Electrical and all-systems physical layout with inspections, Job workflow with hypothesis ledger, MES-style Modules view, Tools page, Timeline, Media (incl. audio), Parts, Feedback and Inbox, printable report and PDFs, others' experience links.\n201\t+- Systems layer (25 systems), Electrical and all-systems physical layout with inspections, Job workflow with hypothesis ledger, MES-style Modules view, Tools page, Timeline, Media (incl. audio), Parts, Feedback and Inbox, printable report and PDFs, others' experience links (2026-10-07).\n202\t+- Tests surface (platform-wide mechanic test catalogue, sourced pass criteria) and Systems dive-in phase 1 (`/v/{vin}/systems/{key}`: status, relationship ring, fault tree, this car's history) (2026-10-08).\n203\t+- Systems map overlay phases 2-4: colour state, hot edges, session time slider, live overlay (`/api/systems/{vin}/state`, `/live`) (2026-10-08/13).\n204\t+- Case memory: closing a Job records a Case; `cases.match`/`cases.prefill` rank real cases above the seed data and feed Job prefill (2026-10-13).\n205\t+- Marque port: `data-marque` computed per-request from the VIN (`marque_for_vin`), model-specific wording in the knowledge tables, Maserati fixture test (2026-10-13).\n206\t+- Tell CUORE mobile (`/m/{vin}`) rebuilt to the Ferrari benchmark: dark, intro reveal every open, 4 quick actions, 3-tap fill-up, camera + Snap & fill on every form; mobile API contract documented for a future native app (2026-10-13).\n207\t+- Live link: first real reads from the car -- active-probe fix for the gateway-silent bus, the 29-bit legislated route, the STFAC filter-reset fix (see 05-methods-and-gotchas.md); full-scan orchestrator, Scans log area with diff/export, scan health report generator, Live board freeze-frame panel, Test A in the Tests catalogue (2026-10-13).\n208\t+- Perf: workup/flow-state results shared across Report/Job/Tests/Timeline via one cache key (Report 30 s -> 5 s, Job 3.2 s -> 0.3 s) (2026-10-13).\n209\t \n210\t ## Next\n211\t \n212\t-1. Use it on the Stelvio: open a Job, record the wiTECH flash check and Test A results, tick the EVAP checklist, attach photos and sounds, answer the Inbox.\n213\t-2. Fill known gaps with sources: EVAP purge and vapour-pressure limits, peak boost, tyre placard pressures, P052E/P04DB, UNKNOWN torques; Grecale and Levante experience links and parts; part images for the remaining 15 parts.\n214\t-3. Timeline: a media and inspections lane; replay of a recording on the gauges from the timeline.\n215\t-4. Live: Mode $06 EVAP test values; MIL state from live reads into the timeline; verify-repair flow end to end on the car.\n216\t-5. Labels: confirm Avery 6576/6578 margins from a print, then mark them verified.\n217\t-6. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, brand accent as a theme variable, experience and parts tables per marque. Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n218\t-7. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n219\t+1. First guided scan with the cables in hand: run the `/coverage` wizard (and a full scan) on the real Stelvio, not a temp-state server, now that the live link actually works on this car.\n220\t+2. Test A (hand vacuum on the ESIM while watching the switch PID), now that Mode $06 has shown the first direct measurement behind the chronic P0440/P0455 (0.090\" leak test FAILED, 404 ms vs a 3965 ms minimum) -- then the wiTECH flash comparison. Do not clear codes first.\n221\t+3. UDS DID definitions from TechAuthority: the module sweep found live codes and module identities but several DIDs are still read raw/UNKNOWN (no decoder in the registry); get real TechAuthority values in rather than guessing.\n222\t+4. Native app: the owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode; `/m/{vin}` and `docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md` are the reference implementation and contract -- Location Services, a pump shortcut and push belong to the native app, not the web page.\n223\t+5. Fill known gaps with sources: EVAP purge and vapour-pressure limits, peak boost, tyre placard pressures, P052E/P04DB, UNKNOWN torques; Grecale and Levante experience links and parts; part images for the remaining 15 parts.\n224\t+6. Timeline: a media and inspections lane; replay of a recording on the gauges from the timeline.\n225\t+7. Labels: confirm Avery 6576/6578 margins from a print, then mark them verified.\n226\t+8. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, experience and parts tables per marque (the theme variable and VIN-based marque detection are now built; data population is what's left). Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n227\t+9. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n228\t+10. Still on the owner (unchanged from the 2026-10-13 session record): readiness read in the 15-85% fuel window (now done once, repeat for any re-test), wiTECH flash check, recalls, service ledger entries (odometer, oil, filter, technician).\n229\t \n230\t ## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\n231\t \n232\t\n233\t"}]},"uuid":"04a1a1c0-2046-4a6f-9015-0915ce0c8e6e","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:07:58.551Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\tool-results\\bzhr1r7s5.txt","content":"########## 01-decisions-and-rules.md ##########\n--- docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md\t2026-10-08 05:50:48.560112800 -0400\n+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:25.967579500 -0400\n@@ -1,29 +1,36 @@\n-# Decisions and rules\n-\n-## Core directive (check every feature against this)\n-\n-CUORE is a diagnostic assistant for a mechanic who specialises in one brand and model. Its job is to help him diagnose this car on evidence, prove the repair, and make the next same-model car with the same fault start from what this one taught. The mechanic decides; CUORE advises and records, with sources, dates and confidence. Before building anything, ask: does it serve diagnosing, proving, or learning for the next car? If not, do not build it. No boards, throughput, blocking gates or inventory management.\n-\n-## Owner's standing rules (2026-09 to 2026-10)\n-\n-1. The mechanic makes the decisions and the repairs. CUORE supplies the most recent, truthful information with date, source and confidence, labels stale or unverified items, and never invents values.\n-2. Others' experience matters: every code, family and job carries verified YouTube how-tos and direct forum threads. Forums block plain HTTP checks, so links are verified through a real browser (headless Edge over the DevTools Protocol).\n-3. Images (photos, scans, borescope video) and audio clips (what a bearing sounds and feels like) are first-class evidence: easy to upload, keep, search and recover.\n-4. Parts need full detail and images; part sites block automated image checks, so images are verified through the browser and linked, never copied.\n-5. More interactivity: the mechanic can correct, question, confirm or add input on any fact and see the answer; an Inbox per car tracks it.\n-6. Systems (25 of them, electrical first) are a correlational dimension for every issue: code to system mapping, dependencies, co-occurrence over time, and the physical layout (wiring, connectors, grounds, boxes, components, locations, conditions) per problem.\n-7. Align CUORE with a mechanic's technical tool like MultiEcuScan: one logical flow tying driver input, mechanic input, test results and malfunctions together (Job workflow, MES-style Modules view).\n-8. Printed pages and PDFs must be properly formatted, with an \"as of\" stamp and sources.\n-9. Branding: Alfa Romeo first; later ported to Alfa, Maserati and Ferrari. Keep marque specifics in data and config. The Stelvio's sibling cars are the Maserati Grecale (shares the Giorgio platform and GME 2.0T engine family) and Levante (different platform, component-level overlap only).\n-10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n-\n-## Design decisions\n-\n-- Safety: no HTTP route ever writes to the car. Clears, actuator tests and routines are MCP-only, need an exact consent phrase (CLEAR <MODULE>, ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>, RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>), and are refused on blocked modules (ABS, EPS, ORC, HALF, DASM, ESL, TVM, TCM, ESM, DTCM, RFHUB, anything on CAN-CH). The live poller only reads (OBD Mode 01/03/07, UDS 0x22) and every other adapter operation is refused while it holds the port.\n-- Evidence: the evidence gate counts only measurements from the car (serial stream). Replay, demo, snapshots, symptoms, notes, feedback, media and inspections are labelled and excluded as measurements. Clearing is not fixing: the verdict stays \"unverified repair\" until a readiness read from the car shows the monitor complete with no code back.\n-- Verdict and status are computed, never hand-written: ACTIVE FAULTS, UNVERIFIED REPAIR, VERIFIED CLEAN, NO DATA; per code ACTIVE, CLEARED UNVERIFIED, STALE.\n-- Known-good bands: only one-sided limits (too hot) become gauge warn/alarm bands; idle-only or two-sided ranges show as notes; UNKNOWN stays blank.\n-- Dossier structure (from the mechanic UX review, implemented 2026-10-07): verdict first, open-work job cards with shared tick state, everything else collapsed with counts, one sticky strip of about 104 px, 16 px body, 44 px targets, dark theme toggle, quick-add note button.\n-- Family findings: several EVAP codes are one fault; three or more lost-communication codes are one power or bus event (supply and grounds first).\n-- Recordings stay in MultiEcuScan's CSV format so the existing log tools read them unchanged.\n-- CUORE runs offline on loopback, kept alive by a per-user scheduled task; no network or Claude dependency.\n+# Decisions and rules\n+\n+## Core directive (check every feature against this)\n+\n+CUORE is a diagnostic assistant for a mechanic who specialises in one brand and model. Its job is to help him diagnose this car on evidence, prove the repair, and make the next same-model car with the same fault start from what this one taught. The mechanic decides; CUORE advises and records, with sources, dates and confidence. Before building anything, ask: does it serve diagnosing, proving, or learning for the next car? If not, do not build it. No boards, throughput, blocking gates or inventory management.\n+\n+## Owner's standing rules (2026-09 to 2026-10)\n+\n+1. The mechanic makes the decisions and the repairs. CUORE supplies the most recent, truthful information with date, source and confidence, labels stale or unverified items, and never invents values.\n+2. Others' experience matters: every code, family and job carries verified YouTube how-tos and direct forum threads. Forums block plain HTTP checks, so links are verified through a real browser (headless Edge over the DevTools Protocol).\n+3. Images (photos, scans, borescope video) and audio clips (what a bearing sounds and feels like) are first-class evidence: easy to upload, keep, search and recover.\n+4. Parts need full detail and images; part sites block automated image checks, so images are verified through the browser and linked, never copied.\n+5. More interactivity: the mechanic can correct, question, confirm or add input on any fact and see the answer; an Inbox per car tracks it.\n+6. Systems (25 of them, electrical first) are a correlational dimension for every issue: code to system mapping, dependencies, co-occurrence over time, and the physical layout (wiring, connectors, grounds, boxes, components, locations, conditions) per problem.\n+7. Align CUORE with a mechanic's technical tool like MultiEcuScan: one logical flow tying driver input, mechanic input, test results and malfunctions together (Job workflow, MES-style Modules view).\n+8. Printed pages and PDFs must be properly formatted, with an \"as of\" stamp and sources.\n+9. Branding: Alfa Romeo first; later ported to Alfa, Maserati and Ferrari. Keep marque specifics in data and config. The Stelvio's sibling cars are the Maserati Grecale (shares the Giorgio platform and GME 2.0T engine family) and Levante (different platform, component-level overlap only).\n+10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n+\n+## Owner's standing rules added 2026-10-13\n+\n+11. Fable (the top-level model) does analysis and decisions only -- it never builds. All building goes to Sonnet/Haiku agents, at most about five running concurrently, and the whole working set stays at roughly half the main model's own token budget. (Also in Claude memory: \"Low-cost subagents only\" -- haiku/sonnet for Agent calls, never Fable forks.)\n+12. About ten complete (full-vehicle) scans over the course of one diagnosis is the right order of magnitude -- not one scan per question. One guided scan (the `/coverage` cable wizard, or a full scan) per shop visit, not per code or per hypothesis.\n+13. Mobile is held to the same standard as the main app: the Ferrari benchmark, not a form. Design and finish matter there exactly as much as on the bench pages -- dark theme, an intro reveal on every open, a camera on every form, prestige over utility-app defaults. (Tell CUORE's first pass was rejected and rebuilt to this standard, 2026-10-13.)\n+14. The photo-reading (vision) provider stays off by default (`CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=none`) because CUORE runs offline by rule. Turning on the `claude` provider is the owner's own explicit, informed opt-in -- it is the one path in the app that deliberately leaves the LAN and sends data (a photo) to Anthropic -- never a default, never silently enabled by another feature.\n+\n+## Design decisions\n+\n+- Safety: no HTTP route ever writes to the car. Clears, actuator tests and routines are MCP-only, need an exact consent phrase (CLEAR <MODULE>, ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>, RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>), and are refused on blocked modules (ABS, EPS, ORC, HALF, DASM, ESL, TVM, TCM, ESM, DTCM, RFHUB, anything on CAN-CH). The live poller only reads (OBD Mode 01/03/07, UDS 0x22) and every other adapter operation is refused while it holds the port.\n+- Evidence: the evidence gate counts only measurements from the car (serial stream). Replay, demo, snapshots, symptoms, notes, feedback, media and inspections are labelled and excluded as measurements. Clearing is not fixing: the verdict stays \"unverified repair\" until a readiness read from the car shows the monitor complete with no code back.\n+- Verdict and status are computed, never hand-written: ACTIVE FAULTS, UNVERIFIED REPAIR, VERIFIED CLEAN, NO DATA; per code ACTIVE, CLEARED UNVERIFIED, STALE.\n+- Known-good bands: only one-sided limits (too hot) become gauge warn/alarm bands; idle-only or two-sided ranges show as notes; UNKNOWN stays blank.\n+- Dossier structure (from the mechanic UX review, implemented 2026-10-07): verdict first, open-work job cards with shared tick state, everything else collapsed with counts, one sticky strip of about 104 px, 16 px body, 44 px targets, dark theme toggle, quick-add note button.\n+- Family findings: several EVAP codes are one fault; three or more lost-communication codes are one power or bus event (supply and grounds first).\n+- Recordings stay in MultiEcuScan's CSV format so the existing log tools read them unchanged.\n+- CUORE runs offline on loopback, kept alive by a per-user scheduled task; no network or Claude dependency.\n\n########## 02-architecture.md ##########\n--- docs/handbook/02-architecture.md\t2026-10-07 23:28:56.695246000 -0400\n+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/02-architecture.md\t2026-10-13 22:04:48.174823800 -0400\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Architecture\n \n-Generated from the code on 2026-10-07. Re-run the greps noted inline if this drifts.\n+Generated from the code on 2026-10-07, refreshed 2026-10-13. Re-run the greps noted inline if this drifts.\n \n ## The three programs\n \n@@ -64,13 +64,27 @@\n | Report | `/v/{vin}/report` | `cuore/web/report_routes.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `timeline_bridge`, `experience_bridge`, `parts_bridge` | `report.html` | `cuore/tests/check_report.py` |\n | Inbox | `/v/{vin}/inbox` | `cuore/web/inbox_routes.py` | `feedback_bridge` | `inbox.html`, `_feedback_panel.html` | `cuore/tests/check_feedback_page.py`, `check_feedback.py` |\n | Logs (link, not a `/v/` tab) | `/logs?vin={vin}` | `cuore/web/routes.py` | `mes_bridge` | `logs.html` | -- |\n+| Tests (2026-10-08, visible tab) | `/v/{vin}/tests` | `cuore/web/tests_routes.py` | `tests_bridge` (via `GET /api/tests/{vin}`) | `tests.html` | `cuore/tests/check_tests_page.py` |\n+| Scans (2026-10-13) | `/v/{vin}/scans`, `/v/{vin}/scans/{scan_id}` | `cuore/web/scanlog_routes.py` | `scanlog_bridge` over `cuore/live/scanlog.py` (groups `observations.jsonl` into sessions, writes nothing) | `scanlog.html`, `scan.html` | `cuore/tests/check_scanlog_page.py` |\n+| Health report (2026-10-13, link from Scans, not its own vbar tab) | `/v/{vin}/health`, `/v/{vin}/scans/{scan_id}/health` | `cuore/web/scan_health_routes.py` | `scan_health_bridge` | `scan_health.html` | `cuore/tests/check_scan_health.py` |\n \n-Not on the vbar but under `/v/{vin}/...`: `verify` (`dossier_routes.py`), `oil-change`/`service`/`brakes-tires`/`torque`/`maintenance` (`service_routes.py`), `drivetrain/{section}` (`drivetrain_routes.py`), `labels`/`labels.pdf` (`labels_routes.py`), `notes` (`routes.py`), `dealer` (`routes.py`), `live-vs-log` (`routes.py`).\n+Vehicle tab strip is now `cuore/web/templates/_vtabs.html` (included from `_vbar.html`), not the old inline list: visible row is Bench, Job, Codes, Live (liveboard), Tests, Systems, Report, Mobile; everything else (Dossier, Modules, Timeline, Gauges, Electrical, Parts, Media, Service, Fault tree, Evidence gate, Inbox, Labels, Logs, Scans, Dashboard, plus a plain link to Tell CUORE) sits behind \"More...\". Health report and the Systems dive-in (`/v/{vin}/systems/{key}`, below) are reached by links from Scans/Systems, not tab entries of their own.\n+\n+Not on the vbar but under `/v/{vin}/...`: `verify` (`dossier_routes.py`), `oil-change`/`service`/`brakes-tires`/`torque`/`maintenance` (`service_routes.py`), `drivetrain/{section}` (`drivetrain_routes.py`), `labels`/`labels.pdf` (`labels_routes.py`), `notes` (`routes.py`), `dealer` (`routes.py`), `live-vs-log` (`routes.py`), `systems/{key}` (`cuore/web/system_routes.py` -- Systems dive-in phase 1, per-system status/relationship ring/fault tree page built from `cuore/services/system_detail_bridge.py`).\n+\n+## Mobile companion: Tell CUORE (`/m/{vin}`), 2026-10-13\n+\n+`cuore/web/owner_routes.py` -- its own phone-first layout (own `Jinja2Templates`, `m_*.html` templates, no desktop chrome), rebuilt 2026-10-13 to the \"Ferrari benchmark\" (dark, intro reveal every open, hero with odometer/verdict, four quick actions, 3-tap fill-up, camera on every form). Routes: `GET /m/{vin}`, `/add`, `/add/{category}`, `/add/{category}/{kind}` (+ `POST`), `/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}`, `/snap` (+ `POST`), `/messages` (+ reply `POST`), `/history`, `/qr`.\n+\n+Every record it writes is **attested, never a car measurement** -- backed by `cuore/live/owner_events.py` (taxonomy: 9 categories, 62 kinds) via `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`, exposed at `/api/owner/{vin}/taxonomy`, `/events` (GET/POST), `/messages` (GET, reply POST), `/correlations` (`cuore/api/owner_events.py`). No route in this chain ever reaches `cuore.live.actuate`/`clear`/`learn`.\n+\n+\"Snap & fill\" photo reading: `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` (`cuore/api/vision.py` -> `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py`), provider `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` = `none` (default, offline) | `claude` (opt-in, sends the photo to Anthropic) | `tesseract` (probe stub, nothing installed). Every value returned is a suggestion a human confirms; a confirmed value saved from a photo is stamped `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`. `docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md` is the documented contract for a future Swift/Flutter app, guarded by `check_api_contract.py`.\n \n ## API router files (`cuore/api/*.py`)\n \n | File | Prefix | Purpose (from docstring) |\n |---|---|---|\n+| `cases.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /vehicles/{vin}/cases/match`, `/cases/prefill` -- case memory read-only, via `cases_bridge` -> `mes.cases` |\n | `checklists.py` | `/api` | Shop-visible checklist state over HTTP: GET/POST one step at a time |\n | `deps.py` | n/a | Shared route dependencies (the single shared-token auth) |\n | `dossier.py` | `/api` | `GET /api/vehicles/{vin}/view` -- the redesigned dossier's data as JSON, read-only |\n@@ -79,18 +93,61 @@\n | `feedback.py` | `/api` | Mechanic feedback on a fact cuore showed; mirrors the MCP feedback tools call-for-call |\n | `jobs.py` | `/api` | JSON face of the Job (case) workflow; writes are thin pass-through to the bridge |\n | `known_good.py` | `/api` | `GET /api/live/known-good`: known-good reference bands for live channels |\n-| `live.py` | `/api` | The live link over HTTP; no write route, read-only UDS allowlist enforced |\n+| `live.py` | `/api` | The live link over HTTP; no write route, read-only UDS allowlist enforced; also hosts `/live/fullscan`, `/live/fullscan/last`, `/live/capture`, `/live/learn/*` (below) |\n | `live_ui.py` | `/api` | Layouts, replay, custom channels, snapshots and triggers for the live-data dashboard UI |\n | `logs.py` | `/api` | Raw log access: index, one file verbatim, regex search (filename-resolution security note) |\n | `media.py` | `/api` | Mechanic evidence media library: upload, browse, recover photos/scans/clips |\n+| `owner_events.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | HTTP face of Tell CUORE (`/owner/{vin}/taxonomy`, `/events`, `/messages`, `/correlations`); every row attested, no route reaches the car |\n | `parts.py` | `/api` | Parts catalog (names, numbers, supersessions, torque, price, images) |\n | `recordings.py` | `/api` | CSV recordings from MES's graph subsystem; only MES output with real per-sample timestamps |\n | `reference.py` | `/api` | Static reference data: module registry and failure-type table |\n+| `scan_health.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /scans/{vin}/{scan_id}/health`(`.md`), `POST .../health/save` -- the scan health report, via `scan_health_bridge` |\n+| `scanlog.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /{vin}/diff`, `/{vin}/{scan_id}`, `/{vin}/{scan_id}/export` -- one scan in full or diffed, exported as JSON or an MES-style log; the only writer, and only under `CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/` |\n | `system.py` | `/api` | Capabilities, health and corpus status; `/api/capabilities` is the first call any client makes |\n | `systems.py` | `/api` | Vehicle-systems graph and DTC-system correlation |\n+| `systems_map.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /systems/{vin}/state` (Systems map overlay: per-system colour, hot edges, session time slider) and `/systems/{vin}/live` (live overlay: worst live colour grade per system, any brand-new DTC); via `systems_map_bridge`, never writes to the car |\n+| `tests.py` (2026-10-08) | `/api` | `GET /tests/catalog`, `/tests/{vin}`, `POST /tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result` -- the mechanic-test catalogue (`mes.mechanic_tests`) and per-VIN results, via `tests_bridge` |\n | `timeline.py` | `/api` | Mechanic-vs-driver timeline: codes on one axis, felt symptoms on the other |\n | `tools.py` | `/api` | Read-only data for the Tools catalogue page; writes to the car listed only as inert cards |\n | `vehicles.py` | `/api` | Per-vehicle diagnostics: the dossier and everything it points at |\n+| `vision.py` (2026-10-13) | `/api` | `GET /vision/status`, `POST /vision/{vin}/read` -- \"read this photo\" for Tell CUORE, via `vision_bridge`; never writes an owner event itself, never touches the car |\n+\n+## Full scan, bus capture and learn (`cuore/live/*`, 2026-10-13)\n+\n+- **Full scan** (`cuore/live/fullscan.py`, `POST /api/live/fullscan`, `GET /api/live/fullscan/last`): one read-only pass over every subsystem the adapter can reach -- OBD DTCs/readiness/Mode $06/Mode $09, every freeze-frame PID, a UDS module sweep with status flags, and a coverage rollup -- sequenced through the existing `cuore/live/ops.py` readers (no new adapter traffic of its own) and recorded as from-car observations so the Scans area, dossier and health report all see it without fifteen separate manual calls. Each step is wrapped so one failure doesn't sink the scan.\n+- **Guided cable wizard** is the pre-existing `/coverage` page (`cuore/web/routes.py`, `coverage.html`, not VIN-scoped itself): a guided three-pass, three-bus session (main bus with no cable, chassis bus through the grey cable, body bus through the blue cable, main bus again) with a bystander diff, backed by `/api/live/coverage*`. Full scan's own `scan_coverage` observation and this wizard's coverage session are two different mechanisms over the same `cuore/live/coverage.py` state.\n+- **Bus capture**: `POST /api/live/capture` (`cuore/live/capture.py`) listens passively (`STCMM 0`, no CAN ACK) and returns the raw frame list; it does **not** persist an observation today -- the frames go back to the caller only.\n+- **Learn**: `cuore/live/learn.py` (pure functions, reconstructs ISO-TP/UDS request-response pairs and DID time series from a passive capture) + `cuore/live/learned.py` (saves accepted mappings to `learned_dids.json`), reached at `POST /api/live/learn/capture`, `/live/learn/correlate`, `/live/learn/accept`, `GET /api/live/learned` -- how a wiTECH capture becomes a DID mapping cuore can read on its own, without ever talking to the adapter itself.\n+- **Live board freeze-frame panel** (`cuore/api/liveboard.py` `/liveboard/{vin}/freeze/capture|status|stop|save|discard`, `cuore/services/liveboard_bridge.py`): starts a capture of stored codes + every supported PID's freeze frame + a Mode 01 snapshot; on save, writes `obd_dtcs`, `freeze_frame`, `pid` (one per channel) and `readiness` observations and hands back a Scans-area scan id.\n+\n+## Observation kinds (`cuore/live/store.py:record_observation`, `observations.jsonl`)\n+\n+No kind is an enum -- any string is accepted; this is what the code actually writes and reads as of 2026-10-13.\n+\n+| Kind | Written by | Read by |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| `adapter_identity` | `fullscan.py` | `dossier_bridge`/health report (adapter/session context) |\n+| `mode09` | `fullscan.py` | scan health report (coverage gaps) |\n+| `obd_dtcs` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` (single reads), `liveboard_bridge.py` (freeze save) | `dossier_bridge`, `scan_health_bridge`, `scanlog.py` (scan grouping) |\n+| `freeze_frame` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py`, `liveboard_bridge.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n+| `readiness` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py`, `liveboard_bridge.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n+| `mode06` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n+| `pids_snapshot` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` |\n+| `pid` | `liveboard_bridge.py` (freeze capture, one per channel) | `scanlog.py` (latest-value-per-PID in a window) |\n+| `module_dtcs` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | `dossier_bridge`, `scan_health_bridge`, `scanlog.py` |\n+| `module_identity` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` |\n+| `did` | `fullscan.py`, `ops.py` | scan health report (DID coverage) |\n+| `scan_coverage` | `fullscan.py` | `scan_health_bridge` (the report's coverage section) |\n+\n+`capture()`'s passive bus listen is not recorded under any kind (see above) -- that is a real gap, not an undocumented one.\n+\n+## Case close-out (2026-10-13 commit 31c0d71)\n+\n+Closing a Job (`cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py:close_job`, step 12) builds and saves a Case (`mes.cases.case_from_job`/`record_case`): confirmed/ruled-out hypotheses, tests run, parts fitted, verification state, pitfalls. `mes.cases.match(vin, codes)`/`prefill(vin, codes)`, exposed read-only at `GET /api/vehicles/{vin}/cases/match` and `/cases/prefill` (`cuore/api/cases.py`, `cuore/services/cases_bridge.py` -- the only module that imports `mes.cases`), rank real recorded cases above the seed data and feed Job prefill from the Systems pages; wording always says \"on the last `<Model>` with these codes\", never presenting a prior car's fix as this car's answer.\n+\n+## Marque theming (`marque_for_vin`, 2026-10-13 commit 003d6a4)\n+\n+`cuore/web/routes.py`'s `_page()` computes `data-marque` once per request from `cuore.services.mes_bridge.marque_for_vin(vin)` (pure passthrough to `mes.platform.marque_for_vin`, confidence-graded VIN-WMI decode: `alfa`/`maserati`/`ferrari`/`unknown`, never guessed) and every `/v/{vin}/*` page inherits it from that one call, instead of each route guessing (previously `data-marque` was hardcoded to `\"alfa\"`).\n \n ## MCP tools\n \n\n########## 05-methods-and-gotchas.md ##########\n--- docs/handbook/05-methods-and-gotchas.md\t2026-10-13 16:59:33.582411500 -0400\n+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/05-methods-and-gotchas.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:14.658971900 -0400\n@@ -11,4 +11,11 @@\n - Git: agent-driven `git push` is blocked by the permission classifier; the owner approves a direct `git push github main`. Remote `forge` is unrelated; never push there.\n - PDF sheets: reportlab in the project venv; render with pypdfium2 and look at the PNG; one US Letter page each; generators live in `docs/vehicles/<VIN>/pdf-sources/`.\n - Serving \"Tell CUORE\" (`/m/{vin}`) to a phone on the shop LAN: the bind setting is `CUORE_HOST` (`cuore/config.py`, default `127.0.0.1`), not a separate `CUORE_BIND` -- one setting already does this, so a second was not added. Setting `CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0` in the keep-alive makes the app reachable from every device on the LAN with **no authentication** unless `CUORE_TOKEN` is also set -- that is the owner's decision, not a default (see `Settings.lan_exposed`/`unguarded_lan`). `GET /m/{vin}/qr` only renders the LAN URL when `lan_exposed` is true; it prints the URL as selectable text (no `qrcode` package in this venv, and a from-scratch QR matrix generator was out of scope) rather than a QR image.\n+- **Three live-layer findings from the first real bench session (2026-10-13, vLinker FS r2 / STN1170 v4.3.2), all fixed in `cuore/live/`:**\n+  1. *Gateway-silent CAN-C needs an active probe.* This car's Security Gateway Module means CAN-C carries no broadcast traffic, so passive listening alone reads as a dead bus. `cuore/live/ops.py:verify_bus` now falls back to an active Mode 01 PID 00 probe (`_active_probe_0100`) before giving up, and marks the bus `verified_by=\"active_probe_0100\"` so later reads know to use the route the probe actually got an answer on.\n+  2. *This car answers legislated OBD only on the 29-bit route.* `18DB33F1 -> 18DAF110` (ECM) / `18DAF118` (TCM), not the 11-bit `7DF`/`7E8` pair -- the opposite of what an earlier (2026-09-25) note on this same car assumed. `cuore/live/ops.py:_obd_route` now prefers whichever STP protocol the active probe was verified against; `cuore/live/transport.py` (session open, ~line 144) restates the 29-bit functional header via `ATCP18`/`ATSHDB33F1`/`ATSTFF` (a single 8-digit `ATSH` is silently ignored by this firmware and leaves the old header in force -- reads as NO DATA, not an error).\n+  3. *`STFAC` on this STN firmware wipes the default pass filters.* After `STFAC` (used when adding custom pass filters, `cuore/live/capture.py:_add_filters`), every reply reads NO DATA because the firmware's default filters are gone too, not just overridden. Fix (`cuore/live/transport.py`, same session-open path, right after the STFAC path runs): re-issue `STCFCPC` + `STP <protocol>` to restore the defaults, then restate the functional header again -- `STP` resets it as well.\n+- **An MCP server process holds the code it started with.** `obd2-mcp/server.py` and `mes-log-mcp/server.py` run as long-lived subprocesses under Claude Code's MCP connection; editing either file does not change what the running tools do until the connection is torn down and rebuilt with the `/mcp` command (reload/reconnect). A code fix that \"doesn't seem to take\" after an edit is usually this, not a real regression -- reload before re-diagnosing.\n+- `cuore/services/cache.py:get_or_build(key, build)` is a small in-process memo cache (16 entries, LRU) keyed on whatever makes the value stale -- never just the VIN. The shared convention across bridges: `(\"workup\", vin, mes_bridge.newest_mtime(vin))` for anything built from the MES log corpus (used by `bench_routes.py`, `flow_bridge.py`, `tests_bridge.py`, `timeline_bridge.py`, `dossier_bridge.py`, `jobs_bridge.py` and others -- this is what took the Report page from 30 s to 5 s and the Job page from 3.2 s to 0.3 s, 2026-10-13); `(\"scan_health\", vin, scan_id, observations.jsonl's mtime)` for the scan health report (`scan_health_bridge.py:build_cached`); `(\"bench_tree_candidates\", vin, codes, mtime)` for the Bench fault-tree view. A new or edited log/observation moves the mtime key component and the stale entry simply falls out -- no invalidation hook needed, but a cache key that forgets to include the right mtime will silently serve a stale page.\n+- Tell CUORE's phone URL moves with the PC's LAN address: cuore binds `CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0` (set in the launchers) and the shop PC is on DHCP, so the IP in the `/m/{vin}/qr` URL (192.168.68.80 as of 2026-10-13; was 192.168.0.161) can change on a reboot or router restart -- check the current address before handing a phone the link, don't assume last session's. The Windows Firewall rule for inbound TCP 5000 needs an admin to run once (`New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"CUORE 5000\" -Direction Inbound -Action Allow -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 5000 -Profile Any`); without it the LAN bind is correct but nothing outside the PC itself can reach the port.\n - \"Read this photo\" (`POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`, `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` + `cuore/api/vision.py`): a value read from a photo is a **suggestion the human confirms**, never a car measurement -- when the confirmed value is saved as an owner event, the caller stamps `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field (same provenance convention `cuore.live.owner_events` already uses) so the record still says it came from a picture, not an instrument. Field names in the response are the real `cuore.live.owner_events.TAXONOMY` field names for the hints that map onto one kind (`fuel_pump` -> `fuel/fill_up`, `oil_bottle` -> `fluids/engine_oil_change`, `part_label` -> `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere`, `receipt` -> `fuel/fill_up`); `odometer` returns `odometer_km` with `suggested_kind: null` because that is the event's own top-level field, not a kind field. Provider is `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` (default `none`, which is deliberately the honest \"not set up, fill in by hand\" answer -- CUORE runs offline by rule, so a vision backend is never silently on). `claude` only turns on with `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` **and** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set -- that call leaves the LAN and goes to Anthropic over plain HTTPS via `urllib` (no `anthropic` SDK in this venv, and none was added), so it is the owner's explicit, informed choice, never a default. `tesseract` is a probe-only stub (`_find_tesseract` checks PATH and `C:\\Program Files\\Tesseract-OCR\\tesseract.exe`); nothing is installed there today and no OCR is wired up behind it. Tests (`cuore/tests/check_vision.py`) monkeypatch `cuore.services.vision_bridge.urllib.request.urlopen` to return a canned Messages-API body rather than calling the real network.\n\n########## 06-roadmap.md ##########\n--- docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md\t2026-10-13 16:54:09.320387500 -0400\n+++ .claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md\t2026-10-13 22:06:50.319653500 -0400\n@@ -1,18 +1,28 @@\n # Roadmap\n \n-## Just built (2026-10-07), to settle in\n+## Done\n \n-Systems layer (25 systems), Electrical and all-systems physical layout with inspections, Job workflow with hypothesis ledger, MES-style Modules view, Tools page, Timeline, Media (incl. audio), Parts, Feedback and Inbox, printable report and PDFs, others' experience links.\n+- Systems layer (25 systems), Electrical and all-systems physical layout with inspections, Job workflow with hypothesis ledger, MES-style Modules view, Tools page, Timeline, Media (incl. audio), Parts, Feedback and Inbox, printable report and PDFs, others' experience links (2026-10-07).\n+- Tests surface (platform-wide mechanic test catalogue, sourced pass criteria) and Systems dive-in phase 1 (`/v/{vin}/systems/{key}`: status, relationship ring, fault tree, this car's history) (2026-10-08).\n+- Systems map overlay phases 2-4: colour state, hot edges, session time slider, live overlay (`/api/systems/{vin}/state`, `/live`) (2026-10-08/13).\n+- Case memory: closing a Job records a Case; `cases.match`/`cases.prefill` rank real cases above the seed data and feed Job prefill (2026-10-13).\n+- Marque port: `data-marque` computed per-request from the VIN (`marque_for_vin`), model-specific wording in the knowledge tables, Maserati fixture test (2026-10-13).\n+- Tell CUORE mobile (`/m/{vin}`) rebuilt to the Ferrari benchmark: dark, intro reveal every open, 4 quick actions, 3-tap fill-up, camera + Snap & fill on every form; mobile API contract documented for a future native app (2026-10-13).\n+- Live link: first real reads from the car -- active-probe fix for the gateway-silent bus, the 29-bit legislated route, the STFAC filter-reset fix (see 05-methods-and-gotchas.md); full-scan orchestrator, Scans log area with diff/export, scan health report generator, Live board freeze-frame panel, Test A in the Tests catalogue (2026-10-13).\n+- Perf: workup/flow-state results shared across Report/Job/Tests/Timeline via one cache key (Report 30 s -> 5 s, Job 3.2 s -> 0.3 s) (2026-10-13).\n \n ## Next\n \n-1. Use it on the Stelvio: open a Job, record the wiTECH flash check and Test A results, tick the EVAP checklist, attach photos and sounds, answer the Inbox.\n-2. Fill known gaps with sources: EVAP purge and vapour-pressure limits, peak boost, tyre placard pressures, P052E/P04DB, UNKNOWN torques; Grecale and Levante experience links and parts; part images for the remaining 15 parts.\n-3. Timeline: a media and inspections lane; replay of a recording on the gauges from the timeline.\n-4. Live: Mode $06 EVAP test values; MIL state from live reads into the timeline; verify-repair flow end to end on the car.\n-5. Labels: confirm Avery 6576/6578 margins from a print, then mark them verified.\n-6. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, brand accent as a theme variable, experience and parts tables per marque. Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n-7. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n+1. First guided scan with the cables in hand: run the `/coverage` wizard (and a full scan) on the real Stelvio, not a temp-state server, now that the live link actually works on this car.\n+2. Test A (hand vacuum on the ESIM while watching the switch PID), now that Mode $06 has shown the first direct measurement behind the chronic P0440/P0455 (0.090\" leak test FAILED, 404 ms vs a 3965 ms minimum) -- then the wiTECH flash comparison. Do not clear codes first.\n+3. UDS DID definitions from TechAuthority: the module sweep found live codes and module identities but several DIDs are still read raw/UNKNOWN (no decoder in the registry); get real TechAuthority values in rather than guessing.\n+4. Native app: the owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode; `/m/{vin}` and `docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md` are the reference implementation and contract -- Location Services, a pump shortcut and push belong to the native app, not the web page.\n+5. Fill known gaps with sources: EVAP purge and vapour-pressure limits, peak boost, tyre placard pressures, P052E/P04DB, UNKNOWN torques; Grecale and Levante experience links and parts; part images for the remaining 15 parts.\n+6. Timeline: a media and inspections lane; replay of a recording on the gauges from the timeline.\n+7. Labels: confirm Avery 6576/6578 margins from a print, then mark them verified.\n+8. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, experience and parts tables per marque (the theme variable and VIN-based marque detection are now built; data population is what's left). Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n+9. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n+10. Still on the owner (unchanged from the 2026-10-13 session record): readiness read in the 15-85% fuel window (now done once, repeat for any re-test), wiTECH flash check, recalls, service ledger entries (odometer, oil, filter, technician).\n \n ## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\n \n\n","numLines":233,"startLine":1,"totalLines":233}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56fa02dd-d1af-41b9-8c51-7531eeacdb23","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
