{"parentUuid":"77fbaaee-3f35-4fcc-a7d7-da0fb12e75f7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1KCdpZ2S3aoePkmxZqc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":177147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2026,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"89488001-292f-4165-b256-a3b8bc73cc5c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg1KCdZgWEuLerx9xKzm2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f1802ee-40a3-43d1-94fd-c8b3c20c22c1","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:08:35.883Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1f1802ee-40a3-43d1-94fd-c8b3c20c22c1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1KCdpZ2S3aoePkmxZqc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JYmBdzKqGnDLy2acQMpKNo","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:/Users/User/mcp-servers/docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md","old_string":"10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n\n## Design decisions","new_string":"10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n\n## Owner's standing rules added 2026-10-13\n\n11. Fable (the top-level model) does analysis and decisions only -- it never builds. All building goes to Sonnet/Haiku agents, at most about five running concurrently, and the whole working set stays at roughly half the main model's own token budget. (Also in Claude memory: \"Low-cost subagents only\" -- haiku/sonnet for Agent calls, never Fable forks.)\n12. About ten complete (full-vehicle) scans over the course of one diagnosis is the right order of magnitude -- not one scan per question. One guided scan (the `/coverage` cable wizard, or a full scan) per shop visit, not per code or per hypothesis.\n13. Mobile is held to the same standard as the main app: the Ferrari benchmark, not a form. Design and finish matter there exactly as much as on the bench pages -- dark theme, an intro reveal on every open, a camera on every form, prestige over utility-app defaults. (Tell CUORE's first pass was rejected and rebuilt to this standard, 2026-10-13.)\n14. The photo-reading (vision) provider stays off by default (`CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=none`) because CUORE runs offline by rule. Turning on the `claude` provider is the owner's own explicit, informed opt-in -- it is the one path in the app that deliberately leaves the LAN and sends data (a photo) to Anthropic -- never a default, never silently enabled by another feature.\n\n## Design decisions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":177147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2026,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JYmBdzKqGnDLy2acQMpKNo":{"file_path":"C:/Users/User/mcp-servers/docs/handbook/01-decisions-and-rules.md","old_string":"10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n\n## Design decisions","new_string":"10. Working method: the main model decides and reviews; low-cost subagents (Sonnet) build. Half the tokens: 4-5 focused checks per feature, one screenshot pass, short reports, one suite run per commit. Commit when agents finish; push only to the `github` remote with the owner's approval; never push to `forge`; never commit koch-mcp/.\n\n## Owner's standing rules added 2026-10-13\n\n11. Fable (the top-level model) does analysis and decisions only -- it never builds. All building goes to Sonnet/Haiku agents, at most about five running concurrently, and the whole working set stays at roughly half the main model's own token budget. (Also in Claude memory: \"Low-cost subagents only\" -- haiku/sonnet for Agent calls, never Fable forks.)\n12. About ten complete (full-vehicle) scans over the course of one diagnosis is the right order of magnitude -- not one scan per question. One guided scan (the `/coverage` cable wizard, or a full scan) per shop visit, not per code or per hypothesis.\n13. Mobile is held to the same standard as the main app: the Ferrari benchmark, not a form. Design and finish matter there exactly as much as on the bench pages -- dark theme, an intro reveal on every open, a camera on every form, prestige over utility-app defaults. (Tell CUORE's first pass was rejected and rebuilt to this standard, 2026-10-13.)\n14. The photo-reading (vision) provider stays off by default (`CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=none`) because CUORE runs offline by rule. Turning on the `claude` provider is the owner's own explicit, informed opt-in -- it is the one path in the app that deliberately leaves the LAN and sends data (a photo) to Anthropic -- never a default, never silently enabled by another feature.\n\n## Design decisions"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"89488001-292f-4165-b256-a3b8bc73cc5c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg1KCdZgWEuLerx9xKzm2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcceee8d-4a88-4b5a-be1d-3e81d7a1f214","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:08:42.879Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
