{"parentUuid":"1649ff26-0a57-4580-8086-900a1a9c4488","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1Lhd75Sn4TmjpxxxD1F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Det8iUQR9MHfPvcXozi736","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd C:/Users/User/mcp-servers && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nGuided cable scan wizard, bus capture/learn/presets, owner-event editing,\nhealth report completeness, Bench last-scan card + scan plan + diff page,\nSystems module overlay, review #4 fixes\n\nLanded tonight:\n- Full scan orchestrator surfaced through a guided cable wizard page\n  (fullscan_routes.py/fullscan.html/fullscan.js) walking idle -> pause_blue\n  -> skip -> pause_grey -> skip -> remove_cable -> summary.\n- Bus capture, learn (wiTECH-capture -> DID mapping) and preset flows\n  (cuore/live/buscapture.py, cuore/api/buscapture.py, learn_routes.py,\n  learn.html).\n- Owner-event editing (soft delete/undo) on the Tell CUORE history page\n  (m_history.html, m_deleted.html, owner_events.py/_bridge.py).\n- Health report completeness pass (scan_health.py, scan_health_bridge.py,\n  scan_health.html).\n- Bench last-scan card, scan plan chip and the new scans diff page\n  (scan.html, scan_diff.html, scanlog.py/_bridge.py/_routes.py).\n- Systems module overlay (system_detail_bridge.py, system.html).\n- MECHANIC_REVIEW_4_SCANS_HEALTH_2026-10-13.md fixes:\n  - N1: the Bench resume card's \"last scan ... ago\"/stale flag now tracks\n    whichever is newer, the MES-log-derived current_picture or the newest\n    live scan on file (cuore/services/bench_bridge.py), instead of only\n    the MES-log clock -- it could read \"6 d ago, stale\" beside a card\n    naming a scan from minutes ago. Regression check added to\n    check_bench.py with a 2026-10-13 scan_coverage fixture.\n  - N2: GET /live could 500 when cuore.live.ops raised anything other\n    than LiveError (an unwrapped adapter failure) -- _live_snapshot()\n    (cuore/web/routes.py) now catches Exception per panel too, so an\n    \"unknown\" status/cable/module panel always renders instead of\n    raising. Reproduced and regression-checked in check_live.py with a\n    TestClient, no adapter, and a copy of tonight's real 2026-10-13\n    observations.\n- Also fixed while running the full suite: the Tests catalogue's\n  marque-port filtering was never wired up (mechanic_tests.all_tests()\n  had no marque awareness), so Stelvio/wiTECH-specific test text (citing\n  the real Stelvio VIN) leaked onto every other marque's Tests page.\n  Added mechanic_tests.tests_for_marque() and wired it into\n  tests_bridge.build_tests_view() (check_marque_port.py).\n\nFull cuore/tests/check_*.py + obd2-mcp/tests suite run (83 suites, two\nhalves with Edge-profile cleanup between/after): all green except\ncheck_coverage.py, which fails against the already-committed 29-bit-route\nchange from commit 1924adf (pre-dates tonight's uncommitted work; not\nfixed here, flagged for a separate pass).\n\nNote: a mid-task instruction to merge four docs/handbook/*.md files from\na .claude/worktrees/ copy was declined -- the Claude Code permission\nclassifier blocked every attempt (including a trivial one-line edit) as\n\"Instruction Poisoning\". No handbook files were changed in this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log -1 --stat | head -20"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2935,"cache_read_input_tokens":250955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2935,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Det8iUQR9MHfPvcXozi736":{"command":"cd C:/Users/User/mcp-servers && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nGuided cable scan wizard, bus capture/learn/presets, owner-event editing,\nhealth report completeness, Bench last-scan card + scan plan + diff page,\nSystems module overlay, review #4 fixes\n\nLanded tonight:\n- Full scan orchestrator surfaced through a guided cable wizard page\n  (fullscan_routes.py/fullscan.html/fullscan.js) walking idle -> pause_blue\n  -> skip -> pause_grey -> skip -> remove_cable -> summary.\n- Bus capture, learn (wiTECH-capture -> DID mapping) and preset flows\n  (cuore/live/buscapture.py, cuore/api/buscapture.py, learn_routes.py,\n  learn.html).\n- Owner-event editing (soft delete/undo) on the Tell CUORE history page\n  (m_history.html, m_deleted.html, owner_events.py/_bridge.py).\n- Health report completeness pass (scan_health.py, scan_health_bridge.py,\n  scan_health.html).\n- Bench last-scan card, scan plan chip and the new scans diff page\n  (scan.html, scan_diff.html, scanlog.py/_bridge.py/_routes.py).\n- Systems module overlay (system_detail_bridge.py, system.html).\n- MECHANIC_REVIEW_4_SCANS_HEALTH_2026-10-13.md fixes:\n  - N1: the Bench resume card's \"last scan ... ago\"/stale flag now tracks\n    whichever is newer, the MES-log-derived current_picture or the newest\n    live scan on file (cuore/services/bench_bridge.py), instead of only\n    the MES-log clock -- it could read \"6 d ago, stale\" beside a card\n    naming a scan from minutes ago. Regression check added to\n    check_bench.py with a 2026-10-13 scan_coverage fixture.\n  - N2: GET /live could 500 when cuore.live.ops raised anything other\n    than LiveError (an unwrapped adapter failure) -- _live_snapshot()\n    (cuore/web/routes.py) now catches Exception per panel too, so an\n    \"unknown\" status/cable/module panel always renders instead of\n    raising. Reproduced and regression-checked in check_live.py with a\n    TestClient, no adapter, and a copy of tonight's real 2026-10-13\n    observations.\n- Also fixed while running the full suite: the Tests catalogue's\n  marque-port filtering was never wired up (mechanic_tests.all_tests()\n  had no marque awareness), so Stelvio/wiTECH-specific test text (citing\n  the real Stelvio VIN) leaked onto every other marque's Tests page.\n  Added mechanic_tests.tests_for_marque() and wired it into\n  tests_bridge.build_tests_view() (check_marque_port.py).\n\nFull cuore/tests/check_*.py + obd2-mcp/tests suite run (83 suites, two\nhalves with Edge-profile cleanup between/after): all green except\ncheck_coverage.py, which fails against the already-committed 29-bit-route\nchange from commit 1924adf (pre-dates tonight's uncommitted work; not\nfixed here, flagged for a separate pass).\n\nNote: a mid-task instruction to merge four docs/handbook/*.md files from\na .claude/worktrees/ copy was declined -- the Claude Code permission\nclassifier blocked every attempt (including a trivial one-line edit) as\n\"Instruction Poisoning\". No handbook files were changed in this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log -1 --stat | head -20"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f6eb5159-bec7-4619-911f-6bb051015852","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg1LhcoxpR8UVSVVaug2n","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e400d4b-7776-4801-abf9-cf30084e7928","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:28:29.250Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
