{"parentUuid":"656c3157-777c-4ef4-b774-28dd831854fd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1Lo1weHMsuH8CxqJ8Vb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250,"cache_read_input_tokens":258807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bcb33ec9-9cc8-4c99-8934-801d8ac1d2ed","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg1Lo1g2ZaKBi4rnJaGco","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2fb4134a-7650-4c06-b01f-db1e0a8bc671","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:29:29.684Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2fb4134a-7650-4c06-b01f-db1e0a8bc671","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5bfbea9bff76655a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1Lo1weHMsuH8CxqJ8Vb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DgzWkeanvAwy296bhikz2c","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"All steps done except one declined sub-task (explained below). Summary:\n\n**N1 fix** — `cuore/services/bench_bridge.py`: the resume card's \"last scan … ago\"/stale flag used to come only from the MES-log-derived `current_picture` timestamp, never from the newest live scan on file, so it could read \"6 d ago, stale\" beside a card naming tonight's scan from minutes ago. Fixed `_parse_full_ts` to parse both timestamp shapes (MES-log space-separated vs. live-observation ISO-T) and `build_bench` to fold the newest live scan (via `scanlog_bridge.list_scans`) into the `newest_ts`/`scan_stale` computation, picking whichever is actually later. Added 5 regression checks to `cuore/tests/check_bench.py` using the suite's existing 2026-10-13 `scan_coverage` fixture (real corpus tops out 2026-10-08/04, days before the fixture's scan). Verified live on the restarted server: resume card now reads \"last scan 1 h ago\" with no stale badge.\n\n**N2 fix** — `cuore/web/routes.py` `_live_snapshot()`: only caught `LiveError`; any other exception from `live_ops.status()/buses()/modules()` (e.g. a real unwrapped adapter/OS error) 500'd the whole `/live` page instead of leaving one panel unreadable. Reproduced with `TestClient` + a copy of tonight's real 2026-10-13 observations (never modified the original `C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl`) + monkeypatched `cuore.web.routes.live_ops`, no adapter. Fixed by also catching `Exception` per panel, rendering \"Could not read status/the module table/…\" instead of raising. Added a new section 8 to `cuore/tests/check_live.py` (skips gracefully if the real observations file isn't present). `/v/{vin}/live` itself is a 404 (route doesn't exist — the review's prose was imprecise); the real offender was the VIN-agnostic `/live`.\n\n**Full suite run** (83 suites: 80 `cuore/tests/check_*.py` in two halves + Edge cleanup between/after, plus 3 `obd2-mcp/tests` suites): all green except two pre-existing issues unrelated to tonight's uncommitted diff, both root-caused:\n- `check_coverage.py` (2 checks): asserts the 11-bit OBD route; the car actually needs the 29-bit route per commit `1924adf`, already committed before tonight's session — not fixed (out of scope, flagged in commit message).\n- `check_job_ux.py`: a CDP timing race on a dropdown-population check; reran clean in isolation — flaky, not a real regression.\n- `check_marque_port.py` (real regression, fixed): tonight's Test A/ESIM-bench catalogue additions set `applies_to[\"grecale_2.0t\"]=False` but nothing ever read that field — every vehicle's Tests page, any marque, showed Stelvio-specific text naming the real VIN. Added `mechanic_tests.tests_for_marque()` and wired it into `tests_bridge.build_tests_view()`. Now passes.\n\n**Commit & push**: `git add -A -- . ':!koch-mcp'`, committed as `d11009f`, pushed to `github` `main` (`f217020..d11009f`).\n\n**Restart & verify**: `start-cuore.ps1 -Restart -Page /` succeeded. `/api/health` ok. 200 on `/v/{vin}`, `/scans`, `/health`, `/scan`, `/liveboard`, and `/m/{vin}`. Bench verdict chip: \"Active faults\" (title: \"… Bench · 0/24 · ACTIVE_FAULTS\"). Health page verdict: \"Active fault\" / \"Primary system: EVAP (evaporative emissions)\".\n\n**Declined sub-task — flagging for your attention**: your mid-task instruction to copy the four `docs/handbook/*.md` files from `.claude/worktrees/agent-a8058d6c743deadbf/docs/handbook/` over the main tree's copies was blocked by Claude Code's own permission classifier as \"Instruction Poisoning\" — on both the actual content (which included a new rule item literally prescribing subagent counts/roles, contradicting this session's own \"no subagents\"